                ENGINE HEALTH MONITORING SYSTEM  (EHM/MRO)
                ==========================================

                RELEASE 4.2C            09-FEB-1996
                POWERPLANT SYSTEMS GROUP, DERBY


1.  WHAT THIS SYSTEM DOES
    ---------------------

    EHM/MRO TAKES THE CRUISE PERFORMANCE SNAPSHOTS DOWNLINKED FROM THE
    FLEET, TRENDS THEM AGAINST THE ENGINE MASTER RECORDS, RAISES THE
    EXCEPTION ALERTS FOR THE DUTY CONTROLLERS AND BUILDS THE WORKSHOP
    INDUCTION PLAN FOR THE OVERHAUL BAYS.

    THE FOUR PRINTED PRODUCTS ARE

        FLEET STATUS SUMMARY        ONE LINE PER ENGINE
        ENGINE ALERT REPORT         EXCEPTIONS ONLY, BY SEVERITY
        WORKSHOP INDUCTION PLAN     ENGINE TO SHOP AND WEEK
        ENGINE HISTORY              ONE ENGINE, WITH THE REPORT DETAIL

    THE SYSTEM RUNS AT A TERMINAL FOR AD HOC ENQUIRIES AND UNDER THE
    OVERNIGHT BATCH JOB (EHMNITE.SH) FOR THE DAILY LISTING.


2.  BUILDING
    --------

        make                    BUILD THE PROGRAM
        make run                RUN THE OVERNIGHT SEQUENCE ON THE
                                SAMPLE DATA IN DATA/ AND WRITE EHM.LIS
        make clean              REMOVE THE OBJECTS AND THE LISTING

    THE SOURCES ARE K AND R C AND BUILD WITH THE STOCK CC ON THE
    OPERATIONS MACHINE.  WHERE THE LOCAL CC DEMANDS FUNCTION
    PROTOTYPES, SET THE DIALECT IN THE MAKEFILE, FOR EXAMPLE

        make CFLAGS="-O -I include -std=c89"

    THE ONLY LIBRARY USED IS THE C RUN TIME LIBRARY.  THERE IS NO
    FLOATING POINT IN THE SYSTEM, ALL ARITHMETIC IS SCALED INTEGER,
    SEE THE COMMENTS AT THE HEAD OF SRC/EHMCALC.C.


3.  RUNNING
    -------

        ehm                     TERMINAL, MENU DRIVEN
        ehm -b                  BATCH, THE FULL OVERNIGHT SEQUENCE
        ehm -d YYMMDD           SET THE RUN DATE
        ehm -f FILE             FLEET MASTER OVERRIDE
        ehm -r FILE             FLIGHT REPORT FILE OVERRIDE
        ehm -s FILE             SLOT FILE OVERRIDE
        ehm -o FILE             WRITE THE PRINTED OUTPUT TO FILE

    THE DATA SETS ARE LOCATED THROUGH THE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE EHMDATA
    (LOGICAL NAME EHM$DATA ON VMS).  IF IT IS NOT SET THE CURRENT
    DIRECTORY IS USED.  THE RUN LOG IS WRITTEN TO EHM.LOG IN THE
    CURRENT DIRECTORY AND IS APPENDED TO, NOT OVERWRITTEN.

    EXIT STATUS IS THE ERROR COUNT, CAPPED AT 63.


4.  FILES
    -----

        Makefile                BUILD RULES
        ehmnite.sh              OVERNIGHT BATCH JOB
        include/ehm.h           TABLES, LIMITS AND ENTRY POINTS
        include/dbio.h          CARD IMAGE COLUMN DEFINITIONS
        src/ehmmain.c           MAIN PROGRAM AND OPERATOR DIALOGUE
        src/dbio.c              DATA SET LOADING, CORE TABLES
        src/ehmcalc.c           TREND CALCULATION AND ALERT RULES
        src/wrkscd.c            WORKSHOP INDUCTION SCHEDULING
        src/rptgen.c            PRINTED OUTPUT, 132 COLUMNS
        src/strutl.c            FIELD AND DATE PRIMITIVES
        src/errlog.c            OPERATOR MESSAGES AND THE RUN LOG
        data/fleet.dat          SAMPLE FLEET MASTER
        data/flights.dat        SAMPLE FLIGHT REPORT EXTRACT
        data/slots.dat          SAMPLE WORKSHOP SLOTS
        doc/filefmt.doc         RECORD LAYOUTS
        doc/message.doc         MESSAGE NUMBERS AND OPERATOR ACTIONS
        doc/opsnote.doc         NOTES FOR THE OPERATIONS ROOM
        HISTORY                 CHANGE HISTORY


5.  KNOWN RESTRICTIONS
    ------------------

    A)  DATES ARE SIX DIGITS, YYMMDD, AND ARE ASSUMED TO LIE IN THE
        NINETEEN HUNDREDS.  SEE DTODAY() IN SRC/STRUTL.C.
    B)  THE FLEET, THE FLIGHT REPORTS AND THE SLOTS ARE HELD IN CORE
        IN FIXED TABLES.  THE LIMITS ARE IN INCLUDE/EHM.H.  EXCEEDING
        A LIMIT PRODUCES A TRUNCATION MESSAGE, NOT AN ABORT.
    C)  THE FLIGHT REPORT FILE IS ASSUMED TO BE IN DATE ORDER WITHIN
        ENGINE.  OUT OF ORDER CARDS ARE LOADED BUT THE HISTORY LISTING
        WILL SHOW THEM AS PRESENTED.
    D)  THERE IS NO WRITE BACK.  THE DATA SETS ARE READ ONLY TO THIS
        SYSTEM, THE MASTERS ARE MAINTAINED BY THE RECORDS OFFICE.
    E)  A CHANGE TO A STRUCTURE IN EHM.H IS A CHANGE TO THE RECORD
        LAYOUT.  COORDINATE WITH THE RECORDS OFFICE BEFORE TOUCHING
        ANYTHING IN THERE.


